173	Quantum soundness of a version of the classical low-degree test for polynomials of low \emph{total} degree was claimed by Natarajan and Vidick, building on an analysis of a three-prover version of the test by Vidick; there is a known gap in the soundness analysis of that test, and it is not used here. Instead, the construction relies on the low \emph{individual} degree test, whose quantum soundness is proved in~\cite{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree} and generalized in~\cite{Ji2021Quantum}. The statement below is the form most directly useful in what follows.
